! STRETCH MAINTENANCE COMPOOL, NOVEMBER 20, 1961
!
! Transcribed from the IBM 7030 Diagnostic Control Program (DCP) manual,
! `docs/ka_ua1_diagnostic_ctl_pgm.pdf`, PDF pp. 129-130 (see
! docs/archival_inventory.md's "Recommended next steps" -- this is that
! work). This is the shared SYN symbol table every other 7030 diagnostic
! deck in bitsavers' diag/ directory references: control-word field
! addresses (ECTL1-4), equipment-availability-word field addresses
! (EQAV1-7), the accumulator-and-friends base (ACA), and one DCP-wide
! base (EDCP1). 65 entries total (51 on p.129, 14 more -- ACA..AIDNTB --
! continuing onto p.130; an earlier pass of archival_inventory.md's
! "51 entries" figure only counted p.129 and needs correcting).
!
! -- Reading the source, and the two format questions this took real
! investigation to pin down --
!
! 1. The glyph between a base symbol and its bit-offset (e.g.
!    "ECTL1&.01" in this degraded 1961 fanfold scan) is the `+`
!    operator. STRAP-1 arithmetic supports only `+`/`-` (C22-6531
!    pp.9-11) -- no other reading is grammatical.
!
! 2. The compiled/resolved-address column this listing prints (e.g.
!    "4006.01&" for EBMAIN) is in a DIFFERENT, OCTAL notation, while
!    STRAP-1 source itself always writes bit addresses in DECIMAL
!    (C22-6531 p.9's "decimal equivalent" describes source notation
!    only). Confirmed exactly against every row: EBBLNK's source offset
!    .46 (decimal) prints as .56 (46 decimal = 56 octal, and the only
!    reading consistent with every other row too -- e.g. ECTL2+.12 ->
!    4007.14, +.19 -> 4007.23, +.28 -> 4007.34, +.51 -> 4007.63,
!    ECTL3+.17 -> 4010.21, EQAV1+.48 -> 4012.60, ACA+8.0 -> 10.00,
!    ACA+13.0 -> 15.00). The word numbers are octal too (control words
!    step 4006, 4007, 4010, 4011 -- octal successors). The trailing `&`
!    glyph after each printed value's two real digits is NOT a third
!    digit at all: it's the *same* ambiguous glyph as the `+` operator,
!    reappearing as a separate, non-numeric per-row mark (most likely a
!    check-bit/parity indicator, plausible for a memory-diagnostic
!    program) -- strip it, it isn't part of the value.
!
! Net effect: this file reproduces the compool's own symbolic
! expressions VERBATIM (decimal offsets, `+` operator, no translation),
! and every printed value below is kept as a trailing comment for
! verify_dcp_maintenance_compool.py to check against, converting this
! model's resolved decimal bit-address back to word.bit-in-octal.
!
! -- Base symbols --
!
! Derived directly from this table's own zero-offset rows (EBAUTO,
! EMACH, EBDRSP's own word less its offset, EBAEC's, EQRDR1, EQPUN1,
! EQTYP1, EQPTR1, EQDIS1, EQTAP1, EQTAP5, and ACA's explicit "SYN,0"),
! each converted from the printed octal word number to decimal:
!   ECTL1 = word 4006(oct) = 2054(dec)      [EBAUTO SYN,ECTL1 -> 4006.00]
!   ECTL2 = word 4007(oct) = 2055(dec)      [EMACH  SYN,ECTL2 -> 4007.00]
!   ECTL3 = word 4010(oct) = 2056(dec)      [EBDRSP SYN,ECTL3+.17 -> 4010.21, offset 17 has no word carry]
!   ECTL4 = word 4011(oct) = 2057(dec)      [EBAEC  SYN,ECTL4+.01 -> 4011.01]
!   EQAV1 = word 4012(oct) = 2058(dec)      [EQRDR1 SYN,EQAV1 -> 4012.00]
!   EQAV2 = word 4013(oct) = 2059(dec)      [EQPUN1 SYN,EQAV2 -> 4013.00]
!   EQAV3 = word 4014(oct) = 2060(dec)      [EQTYP1 SYN,EQAV3 -> 4014.00]
!   EQAV4 = word 4015(oct) = 2061(dec)      [EQPTR1 SYN,EQAV4 -> 4015.00]
!   EQAV5 = word 4016(oct) = 2062(dec)      [EQDIS1 SYN,EQAV5 -> 4016.00]
!   EQAV6 = word 4017(oct) = 2063(dec)      [EQTAP1 SYN,EQAV6 -> 4017.00]
!   EQAV7 = word 4020(oct) = 2064(dec)      [EQTAP5 SYN,EQAV7 -> 4020.00]
!   ACA   = word 0                          [ACA    SYN,0     -- literal, no offset]
!   EDCP1 = word 4000(oct) = 2048(dec)      [EQMEM SYN,EDCP1+21.0 -> 4025.00, so
!                                             EDCP1 = word(4025oct=2069dec) - 21(words) = 2048dec = word 4000(oct).
!                                             Independently corroborated: docs/archival_inventory.md
!                                             already cites the DCP's own memory footprint as starting
!                                             at octal 004000 -- exactly this value.]

ECTL1   SYN, 2054.0
ECTL2   SYN, 2055.0
ECTL3   SYN, 2056.0
ECTL4   SYN, 2057.0
EQAV1   SYN, 2058.0
EQAV2   SYN, 2059.0
EQAV3   SYN, 2060.0
EQAV4   SYN, 2061.0
EQAV5   SYN, 2062.0
EQAV6   SYN, 2063.0
EQAV7   SYN, 2064.0
ACA     SYN, 0
EDCP1   SYN, 2048.0

! -- p.129 body (51 entries) --
!                                          printed (octal word.bit, trailing check mark stripped)
EBAUTO  SYN, ECTL1                      ! 4006.00
EBMAIN  SYN, ECTL1+.01                  ! 4006.01
EBSURV  SYN, ECTL1+.02                  ! 4006.02
EBDCP   SYN, ECTL1+.03                  ! 4006.03
EBMCON  SYN, ECTL1+.04                  ! 4006.04
EBBLNK  SYN, ECTL1+.46                  ! 4006.56
EMACH   SYN, ECTL2                      ! 4007.00
ETAPCM  SYN, ECTL2+.12                  ! 4007.14
ETAPDM  SYN, ECTL2+.19                  ! 4007.23
ETAPCS  SYN, ECTL2+.28                  ! 4007.34
ETAPDS  SYN, ECTL2+.35                  ! 4007.43
ETAPCO  SYN, ECTL2+.44                  ! 4007.54
ETAPDO  SYN, ECTL2+.51                  ! 4007.63
EB16CH  SYN, ECTL2+.61                  ! 4007.75
MNTCTL  SYN, ECTL2+.62                  ! 4007.76   @MAINT CONSL CONTROL
EBDRSP  SYN, ECTL3+.17                  ! 4010.21
EDPLOC  SYN, ECTL3+.32                  ! 4010.40
EBAEC   SYN, ECTL4+.01                  ! 4011.01
EBHARV  SYN, ECTL4+.02                  ! 4011.02
EBK1    SYN, ECTL4+.03                  ! 4011.03
EBK2    SYN, ECTL4+.04                  ! 4011.04
EBK3    SYN, ECTL4+.05                  ! 4011.05
EQRDR1  SYN, EQAV1                      ! 4012.00
EQRDR2  SYN, EQAV1+.16                  ! 4012.20
EQRDR3  SYN, EQAV1+.32                  ! 4012.40
EQRDR4  SYN, EQAV1+.48                  ! 4012.60
EQPUN1  SYN, EQAV2                      ! 4013.00
EQPUN2  SYN, EQAV2+.16                  ! 4013.20
EQPUN3  SYN, EQAV2+.32                  ! 4013.40
EQPUN4  SYN, EQAV2+.48                  ! 4013.60
EQTYP1  SYN, EQAV3                      ! 4014.00
EQTYP2  SYN, EQAV3+.16                  ! 4014.20
EQTYP3  SYN, EQAV3+.32                  ! 4014.40
EQTYP4  SYN, EQAV3+.48                  ! 4014.60
EQPTR1  SYN, EQAV4                      ! 4015.00
EQPTR2  SYN, EQAV4+.16                  ! 4015.20
EQPTR3  SYN, EQAV4+.32                  ! 4015.40
EQPTR4  SYN, EQAV4+.48                  ! 4015.60
EQDIS1  SYN, EQAV5                      ! 4016.00
EQDIS2  SYN, EQAV5+.16                  ! 4016.20
EQDIS3  SYN, EQAV5+.32                  ! 4016.40
EQDIS4  SYN, EQAV5+.48                  ! 4016.60
EQTAP1  SYN, EQAV6                      ! 4017.00
EQTAP2  SYN, EQAV6+.16                  ! 4017.20
EQTAP3  SYN, EQAV6+.32                  ! 4017.40
EQTAP4  SYN, EQAV6+.48                  ! 4017.60
EQTAP5  SYN, EQAV7                      ! 4020.00
EQTAP6  SYN, EQAV7+.16                  ! 4020.20
ETAP7   SYN, EQAV7+.32                  ! 4020.40
EQTAP8  SYN, EQAV7+.48                  ! 4020.60
EQMEM   SYN, EDCP1+21.0                 ! 4025.00

! -- p.130 body (14 more entries, continuing the same table --
! accumulator/adder/identity register field addresses, word-granularity
! offsets from ACA) --
ACB     SYN, ACA+1.0                    ! 1.00
ACC     SYN, ACA+2.0                    ! 2.00
ACD     SYN, ACA+3.0                    ! 3.00
ACE     SYN, ACA+4.0                    ! 4.00
ACF     SYN, ACA+5.0                    ! 5.00
ACG     SYN, ACA+6.0                    ! 6.00
ACH     SYN, ACA+7.0                    ! 7.00
ADA     SYN, ACA+8.0                    ! 10.00
ADB     SYN, ACA+9.0                    ! 11.00
ADC     SYN, ACA+10.0                   ! 12.00
ADD     SYN, ACA+11.0                   ! 13.00
AIDNTA  SYN, ACA+12.0                   ! 14.00
AIDNTB  SYN, ACA+13.0                   ! 15.00
